  <p class="note-line">
    Private polytechnic and diploma colleges typically charge Rs 45,000 to Rs 7,00,000 a year for the
    same category of diploma, depending on institute and specialisation. Figures are directional based
    on current fee-tracking sources at the time of writing; verify current fees directly with the
    specific institute or state technical education board before applying.
  </p>

  <div class="highlight-box highlight-box--amber">
    <p>
      A private-seat premium is only worth paying if it buys something the government seat genuinely
      lacks: verifiably better labs, faculty, or a placement record you can check against real company
      names and pay ranges, not brochure language.
    </p>
  </div>

  <p>
    A simple planning heuristic: treat any single diploma as a rough 10 percent slice of your family's
    total realistic education budget, not the whole pie. A government polytechnic seat sits well inside
    that heuristic on its own. A premium private diploma at Rs 3-7 lakh a year can eat that 10 percent
    fast — which is fine if the specific institute can show a verifiable placement record, real lab or
    clinical access, and named recruiters, but not fine if the only justification is the campus looking
    impressive on a brochure.
  </p>

  <h2 id="diploma-vs-degree">Diploma vs degree after 12th: the honest comparison</h2>

  <p>
    This is the real trade-off underneath "which diploma is best," and it deserves a direct answer
    instead of a vague "it depends."
  </p>

  <div class="table-wrap">
    <table class="paths-table">
      <thead>
        <tr>
          <th>Factor</th>
          <th>Diploma</th>
          <th>Degree</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
